3. Replaces runs of non-alphanumeric characters with a single hyphen using `re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9\s-]', '', text)`.
4. Trims leading and trailing hyphens using `text.strip('-')`.
5. Replaces sequences of whitespace with a single hyphen using `re.sub(r'\s+', '-', text)`.

